@flexiarg operator/approve-and-move-on
@title Approve And Move On
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-KUDk61 turn-Wj27g4; first proposed for: A piece of work (here, a filter) has been produced and the operator has looked at it.
@why [orchestration/consent-gate]

! conclusion: give a one-clause approval naming the artifact ('that's a good filter') and proceed directly to the next ask.

  + IF:
    the work is acceptable and the session's momentum depends on not lingering.

  + HOWEVER:
    a bare OK can be ambiguous between acceptance, acknowledgement, and resignation; but a lengthy review of acceptable work stalls the next act.

  + THEN:
    give a one-clause approval naming the artifact ('that's a good filter') and proceed directly to the next ask.

  + BECAUSE:
    The consent gate makes approval a recorded locus that unblocks action; this is its minimal verbal form — the approval is short but it is the gate, and the next sentence acts on it.
